# OpenTV U-Boot diagnostics probe  --  NON-DESTRUCTIVE / READ-ONLY
#
# Deploy as <FAT32 stick root>/kylo_usb_update.scr, boot holding OK.
# U-Boot (NT72671, 2016.07) sources this plain-text script. It contains
# NO nand/sf ERASE or WRITE and NO nwriteloader/trimffs: it only reads
# flash into RAM and writes result files BACK TO THE USB STICK via
# fatwrite. Nothing touches the TV's NAND/SPI. Pull the stick, read the
# dump_*.bin / *.txt files on a PC. If the format is bad U-Boot aborts
# with no effect. CONFIRMED to execute on hardware 2026-11-12.
#
# Round 1 (done): xbootdat[0:8K]/npt/misc/spi[0:0x20000].
# Round 2 (done): full xbootdat, fdt0, apdat0[0:0xa00000].
# Round 3 (done): SPI[0:0x20000], full xbootdat, fdt0, apdat0[0:0x3c0000]
#   (3.75 MiB prefix only — LEBs are SCATTERED in this vendor UBI, the
#   window missed the layout lnum=0 PEB and the master/data LEBs).
# Round 4 (done): SPI FULL 0..0x40000 (MAC @0x23000 read OK) + apdat0
#   FULL 0xa00000. Result: conf write was LIVE and healthy; root cause
#   of the loop = ntkethmac.ko never loaded in the remote.txt path.
# Round 5 (this file): fs0 head PEB0-7 @0x1fc0000 (volume table of the
#   fs0 UBI: ap0 vol_type + rsvd_pebs - required to plan the Track-C
#   ap0 squashfs patch). fs0 offset 0x1fc0000 anchor-checked against
#   fdt0 @0xac0000 and apdat0 @0xe340000 from the live mtdparts.
#
# RAM scratch 0x3300000 = DRAM load area the stock update script uses.
# NAND offsets are raw mtd0 offsets from the live `mtdparts` env.

echo OPENTV-PROBE v5: begin

# 0) marker: proves a custom .scr ran at all ("NVOK")
mw.l 0x3300000 0x4b4f564e
fatwrite usb 0:auto 0x3300000 opentv_probe_ran.bin 4

# 1) fs0 head, PEB0..7 @0x1fc0000 (2 MiB): UBI volume table (layout
#    volume) -> ap0 volume type/static-or-dynamic + rsvd_pebs capacity
nand read 0x3300000 0x1fc0000 0x200000
fatwrite usb 0:auto 0x3300000 dump_fs0_head.bin 0x200000

echo OPENTV-PROBE v5: done
% <- this is end of file symbol
